WEBVTT

00:04:57.788 --> 00:05:00.038
even though maybe
they'd never been to Chicago.

00:05:00.079 --> 00:05:01.371
It's a good look.

00:05:01.413 --> 00:05:03.371
But let me take you to another Maya city.

00:05:03.413 --> 00:05:05.538
And this is where I work,
called Xunantunich.

00:05:05.579 --> 00:05:08.621
In 2016, archaeologists found
the largest tomb ever discovered

00:05:08.663 --> 00:05:11.621
in the country, in Belize --
that's where Xunantunich is.

00:05:11.663 --> 00:05:15.038
And inside that tomb,
there were the remains of a ruler,

00:05:15.079 --> 00:05:16.329
but also jade,

00:05:16.371 --> 00:05:19.871
the kind of plates and the kind of vessels
that you might see in a museum,

00:05:19.913 --> 00:05:22.829
and jaguar bones, which symbolize
possibly royal power.

00:05:22.871 --> 00:05:26.913
This person may have actually
even been wearing a jaguar pelt cape.

00:05:26.954 --> 00:05:29.079
But Xunantunich was a fairly small city.

00:05:29.121 --> 00:05:32.913
So there was a possibility
that this was a foreign ruler.